<help>
<title>Bell 430</title>
			<key>
				<name>{ }</name>
				<desc>shutdown/start ( to ground idle ! ) turbines</desc>
			</key>
			
			<key>
				<name>i</name>
				<desc>toggle ignition switch</desc>
			</key>
			
			<key>
				<name>n/N</name>
				<desc>engine power adjustment up/down</desc>
			</key>
			
			
			<key>
				<name>MMB</name>
				<desc>adjust power lever (middle mouse button)</desc>
			</key>
			
			<key>
				<name>M/m</name>
				<desc>Raise/lower Winch man ( when available )</desc>
			</key>
			
			<key>
        <name>w</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Up</desc>
      </key>
	  
      <key>
        <name>a</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Left</desc>
      </key>
	  
      <key>
        <name>s</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Down</desc>
      </key>
	  
      <key>
        <name>d</name>
        <desc>Rotate Searchlight Right</desc>
      </key>  
	  
      <key>
        <name>r</name>
        <desc>Activate Winch Man ( see notes below )</desc>
      </key>  
	  <line>If you are using HDR, then you need to enable the specific HDR panel lights from the Bell 340 Menu.</line>
 <line>Using the HDR panel lights while not in HDR will produce very strange results.</line>
			<line> </line>
<line>STARTING THE BELL 430</line>
<line></line>	  
<line>Turn the Battery power ON from the Rocker switch on the Overhead Panel.</line>
<line>All screens etc should now have power.</line>
<line>The 430 has a full Auto start sequence which can be activated by pressing ether of the 2 Engine Start buttons on the main panel.</line>
<line>The Autostart will  take the engines up to ground idle only.</line>
<line>Once ground idle is achieved, turn on Generators 1 + 2 from the Rocker swiches on the Overhead Panel, then Disengage the Battery.</line>
<line>Increase Power to 100% for take off and flight.</line>
<line></line>
<line>Rotorbrake can only be activated by the lever mounted on the bulkhead by the Pilots right arm.</line>	
<line>All external lights are default to OFF and are toggled by the switch panel on the centre console</line>
<line>PITOT heaters are default to OFF and are toggled by the switch panel on the centre console</line>
<line>Search light ( when fitted ) are switched on/off from Night Sun panel  on the centre console.</line>
<line>Parking brake  is  activated  by the Grey lever on the centre console.</line>
<line> The Winch man is only available on winch equipped  load outs. He can only be seen when he has been activated and the door is open..</line>
<line>FLIR view is only available on configurations that contain a FLIR unit.</line>
<line></line>
<line>AUTOPILOT V3 </line>
<line>The Autopilot is now able to control  speed, altitude and heading. Autopilot is only usable  between 30-140kts</line>
<line>Heading modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>Speed modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>****  Altitude modes can only be used in conjunction with speed mode being being active. This includes the use of Vertical Speed mode.  ***</line>
<line>AUTOPILOT ISSUES !!!!!</line>
<line>When disengaging the AP entirely or from a singe mode, the  control inputs will snap to your actual cyclic/colective/pedal positions as soon as you  move any of them.</line>
<line>This is unavoidable as  the sim can not physically move your cyclic/colective/pedal positions to match the Autopilots input.</line>
<line>The best advice to minimise the sudden change of input would be for you to  have your cyclic/colective/pedal positions ready in approximatly correct positions  to minimise the "snap".</line>

</help>
